Windows portability fixes for upstream KRDC, applied by winbuild/ after
krdc-ai.patch. Kept out of the AUR/upstream patch so the AI feature series
stays reviewable on its own; these are pre-existing Windows-only bugs in
upstream code that Linux CI never compiles.

1. rdp/rdpsession.cpp: the _WIN32 WSAStartup block logs with SDL_TAG, a tag
   string private to FreeRDP's SDL client (this block was copy-pasted from
   there). It is not part of FreeRDP's public API; WLog only wants a tag
   string.

2. factorwidget.h: FactorWidget is marked KRDCCORE_EXPORT but factorwidget.cpp
   is compiled into the krdc executable, not krdccore. On Linux the macro is
   just default visibility and the in-executable definition satisfies the
   references. On Windows it becomes __declspec(dllimport), so mainwindow.cpp
   and factorwidget.cpp reference __imp_ thunks that no import library
   provides, and linking fails. Nothing outside the executable uses
   FactorWidget, so the export macro is simply wrong; drop it.

diff --git a/rdp/rdpsession.cpp b/rdp/rdpsession.cpp
--- a/rdp/rdpsession.cpp
+++ b/rdp/rdpsession.cpp
@@ -505,7 +505,9 @@
     const DWORD wVersionRequested = MAKEWORD(1, 1);
     const int rc = WSAStartup(wVersionRequested, &wsaData);
     if (rc != 0) {
-        WLog_ERR(SDL_TAG, "WSAStartup failed with %s [%d]", gai_strerrorA(rc), rc);
+        // SDL_TAG belongs to FreeRDP's SDL client, not to FreeRDP itself;
+        // WLog takes any tag string.
+        WLog_ERR("krdc.rdp", "WSAStartup failed with %s [%d]", gai_strerrorA(rc), rc);
         return false;
     }
 #endif
diff --git a/factorwidget.h b/factorwidget.h
--- a/factorwidget.h
+++ b/factorwidget.h
@@ -17,6 +17,6 @@
  * Widget Action to display slider in the action toolbar. Each time action is
  * add, the new QSlider widget is created via @ref createWidget() method.
  */
-class KRDCCORE_EXPORT FactorWidget : public QWidgetAction
+class FactorWidget : public QWidgetAction
 {
     Q_OBJECT
